Implement module restoring_divide with clk,rst_n and ports {"inputs": [["abort", 1], ["start", 1], ["advance", 1], ["numerator", 4], ["denominator", 4]], "outputs": [["busy", 1], ["done", 1], ["quotient", 4], ["remainder", 4]]}
Specification:
Unsigned 4-bit restoring divider, rising edges only, async active-low reset zeroes all state/output. abort highest priority: busy=done=quotient=remainder=0 and discard work. Otherwise done is a one-edge pulse (default 0 each rising edge). When OLD busy=0, start accepts current numerator/denominator regardless advance: for denominator=0 finish immediately with busy=0,done=1,quotient=15,remainder=numerator; otherwise busy=1, load work, four accepted advance edges required, hold previous quotient/remainder. When OLD busy=1, start and operand changes ignored. advance=0 pauses all work and holds busy/quotient/remainder, done still clears. Each advance shifts next numerator MSB into partial remainder, shifts quotient, conditionally subtracts latched denominator and sets quotient low bit iff trial>=denominator. On the fourth advance publish new quotient/remainder, busy=0,done=1. A start simultaneous with that fourth advance is ignored (OLD busy). No implicit extra advance at acceptance. Falling/stable clock changes hold all output; reset assertion clears immediately, release alone does not act.
Public ordered binary events (clk,rst_n,packed input,packed output; ports packed in listed order; sample after #2):
